  "id": "behavior-shaping",
  "term": "behavior shaping",
  "definition": "Behavior shaping is a way of building a desired behavior by rewarding actions that increasingly resemble the target behavior. Over time, the standard for reward becomes more exact, so only responses that are closer to the goal continue to be reinforced.",
